      "description": "Memorial Patriot Tower in Busan is a monument to commemorate the Korean military, police officers, and warriors from Busan who died after the establishment of the Korean government in 1948. Commissioned by the Busan Metropolitan government in 1980, the tower was built at a height of about 74 meters on Gubong Mountain in 1983. It stands on a circular artificial pond and is characterized by nine walls supporting one circle at the top. Kim took this motif from Nine-story Pagoda at Hwangnyongsa Temple from the Unified Silla period, Korea.",
